Found live on amdlab, 2026-10-31 (image live-20bec47 = 20bec47 + Rex::Rancher 0.005/Rex::GPU 0.006).

`ocp node add synapse --provider ssh-default --host 10.230.30.50 --node_ip 10.230.30.50 --gpu` against a cluster whose CRDs were installed by an older OCP (ocpnodes.ocp.internal created 2026-10-30T23:55, no `nodeIP` in its schema). Result:
- OCPNode spec as stored: `{"gpu":true,"host":"10.230.30.50","providerRef":"ssh-default","role":"worker"}` — no nodeIP; the apiserver pruned the unknown field (structural schema), no error.
- /etc/rancher/rke2/config.yaml on synapse: no `node-ip:` line.
- Node registered InternalIP 192.168.0.165 (default route, eno1) instead of 10.230.30.50 (vlan30).
- Nothing on STDERR about it: no refusal, no mismatch [WARN] (status.nodeIP is never set, so there is nothing to compare).

So k254 does nothing on every existing cluster until something re-applies the CRD (`ocp apply` / `deploy-robocop`), and says nothing — the exact silent failure k254 exists to prevent.

Done = (1) a test with a fake API that prunes nodeIP reproduces it; (2) `ocp node add --node_ip` refuses BEFORE anything is created or provisioned when the cluster cannot store spec.nodeIP — e.g. check the live OCPNode CRD schema for spec.properties.nodeIP, or a server-side dryRun create compared with what was asked — with a diagnosis naming the fix (`ocp apply` updates the CRD); do not silently re-apply the CRD from node add (an older image would downgrade a newer schema); (3) check the same for the other writers of spec.nodeIP (Apply/CR.pm extra control planes and ensure_cp_ocpnode: is ensure_crd guaranteed to run before them?), and state what happens for a hand-written OCPNode on an old CRD (robocop path) — document or detect; (4) the mismatch check should not stay silent when spec.nodeIP was asked for but is absent from the stored CR.

